          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Cayley 4-form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            (
            %a{:href => "#HarveyLawson82"}> Harvey-Lawson 82
            ) is a certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+n-form"} differential 4-form
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} real 8-dimensional space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 8
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^8
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Phi \;\in\; \Omega^4(\mathbb{R}^n)
          %p
            which constitutes an exceptional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calibration"} calibration
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^4
            with its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean geometry
          %p
            More generally, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%287%29-manifold"} Spin(7)-manifold
            carries a globalization of this 4-form
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calibration"} calibration
          %p
            %br/
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#HarveyLawson82"}> Harvey-Lawson 82, Def. 1.21
            )
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h2#invariance Invariance
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizer+subgroup"} stabilizer subgroup
            inside
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} GL(8)
            of the Cayley 4-from under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            given by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+of+differential+forms"} pullback of differential forms
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%287%29"} Spin(7)
            inside
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SO%288%29"} SO(8)
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#HarveyLawson82"}> Harvey-Lawson 82, Prop. 1.36
            )
          %h3#as_a_calibration As a calibration
          %p
            The Cayley 4-form constitutes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calibration"} calibration
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 8
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^8
            (
            %a{:href => "#HarveyLawson82"}> Harvey-Lawson 82
            )
          %h3#GrassmannianOfCayley4Planes Grassmannian of Cayley 4-planes
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calibrated+submanifold"} calibrated submanifold
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            is also called a
            %em Cayley 4-plane
            (not to be confused with the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cayley+plane"} Cayley plane
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#HarveyLawson82"}> Harvey-Lawson 82, Def. 1.23
            )
          %p
            The space (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"}> moduli space
            ) of Cayley 4-planes, denoted
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CAY
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CAY
            (
            %a{:href => "#BryantHarvey89"}> Bryant-Harvey 89, (2.19)
            ) or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CAYLEY
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CAYLEY
            (
            %a{:href => "#GluckMackenzieMorgan95"}> Gluck-Mackenzie-Morgan 95, (5.20)
            ), is hence a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+subspace"} topological subspace
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmannian"} Grassmannian
            of all 4-planes in 8-dimensions:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CAY
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi Gr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 4
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 8
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CAY
                  \\subset
                  Gr(4,8)
          %p
            This is of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
            4 (
            %a{:href => "#HarveyLawson82"}> Harvey-Lawson 82, below (5)
            ). In fact, this space is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphic
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+space"} coset space
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%287%29"} Spin(7)
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%284%29.Spin%283%29"} Spin(4).Spin(3)
            \=
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%283%29.Spin%283%29.Spin%283%29"} Spin(3).Spin(3).Spin(3)
            \=
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sp%281%29.Sp%281%29.Sp%281%29"} Sp(1).Sp(1).Sp(1)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CAY
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 7
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CAY \;\simeq\; Spin(7)/\big( Spin(4) \cdot Spin(3)\big)
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#HarveyLawson82"}> Harvey-Lawson 82, Theorem 1.38
            , see also
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BryantHarvey89"} Bryant-Harvey 89, (3.19)
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#GluckMackenzieMorgan95"} Gluck-Mackenzie-Morgan 95, (5.20)
          %p
            Moreover, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+space"} coset space
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%286%29"} Spin(6)
            by
            %a{:href => "Spn.Sp1#SO4"} Spin(3).Spin(3)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≃
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \simeq
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SO%284%29"} SO(4)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi CAY
                    %mi sL
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 6
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CAY_{sL}
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  Spin(6)/\big( Spin(3) \cdot Spin(3)\big)
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  SU(4)/SO(4)
          %p
            is the Grassmannian of those Cayley 4-planes which are also
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+Lagrangian+submanifolds"} special Lagrangian submanifolds
            (
            %a{:href => "#BBMOOY96"}> BBMOOY 96, p. 7 (8 of 17)
            ).
          %p
            See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "Spn.Sp1#SpinGrassmannians"} Spin Grassmannians
